1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,142
This week I changed what I'm entering.

2
00:00:03,192 --> 00:00:06,334
Confide stays where it was submitted first;

3
00:00:06,384 --> 00:00:13,629
for this fair I moved to the Tempo track, where my Reth and Revm work fits.

4
00:00:13,679 --> 00:00:15,453
The product is Sworn.

5
00:00:15,503 --> 00:00:21,893
On MPP, if a paid answer is wrong, a refund is the server's choice.

6
00:00:21,943 --> 00:00:26,953
Sworn makes the server reserve its own bond behind each answer,

7
00:00:27,003 --> 00:00:32,012
and a zero-knowledge proof of Tempo's own EVM can slash it.

8
00:00:32,062 --> 00:00:38,452
It runs end to end on Tempo's own node, and it's deployed on Moderato.

9
00:00:38,502 --> 00:00:46,682
What I learned: our first full run said "blocked" but the transfer had simply run out of gas

10
00:00:46,732 --> 00:00:49,883
— Tempo prices storage about eleven times Ethereum.

11
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:51,712
The test caught it.

12
00:00:51,762 --> 00:00:54,455
Next: the first slash on Moderato.
